      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-309248",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is true about the values of $4^{x}$ and $4x + 1$ for $x > 0$?\n\n1. There is a constant $c$ such that if $0 < x < c$, then $4^{x} > 4x + 1$, but if $x > c$, then $4^{x} < 4x + 1$.\n2. There is a constant $c$ such that if $0 < x < c$, then $4^{x} < 4x + 1$, but if $x > c$, then $4^{x} > 4x + 1$.\n3. For all $x > 0$, it is true that $4^{x} > 4x + 1$.\n4. For all $x > 0$, it is true that $4^{x} < 4x + 1$."
    },
