      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-309257",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is true about the values of $7x + 3$ and $7^{x}$ for $x > 0$?\n\n1. For all $x > 0$, it is true that $7x + 3 < 7^{x}$.\n2. There is a constant $c$ such that if $0 < x < c$, then $7x + 3 < 7^{x}$, but if $x > c$, then $7^{x} < 7x + 3$.\n3. There is a constant $c$ such that if $0 < x < c$, then $7x + 3 > 7^{x}$, but if $x > c$, then $7^{x} > 7x + 3$.\n4. For all $x > 0$, it is true that $7x + 3 > 7^{x}$."
    }
